{"name":"Little Sun Dress","hex":"#f7c85f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"little","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Small, not large, limited, particularly:","Small, limited in size."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Not much.","Not at all."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/little"},{"term":"sun","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Sundanese."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The star that is closest to the Earth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun"},{"term":"dress","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put clothes (or, formerly, armour) on (oneself or someone, a doll, a mannequin, etc.); to clothe. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To put clothes (or, formerly, armour) on (oneself or someone, a doll, a mannequin, etc.); to clothe. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An item of clothing (usually worn by a woman or young girl) which both covers the upper part of the body and includes a skirt below the waist.","An item of clothing (usually worn by a woman or young girl) which both covers the upper part of the body and includes a skirt below the waist."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dress"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sundress","blocks":[{"text":"A sundress or summer dress is an informal or casual dress intended to be worn in warm weather, typically in a lightweight fabric, most commonly cotton, and usually loose-fitting. It is commonly a bodice-style sleeveless dress, typically with a wide neckline and thin shoulder straps, and may be backless. A sundress is typically worn without a layering top and is not usually worn over a blouse, sweater, or t-shirt, or with leggings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/A_Woman_in_a_Red_Sundress.jpg/330px-A_Woman_in_a_Red_Sundress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sundress","wikidata":"Q7639866"},{"title":"Sun","blocks":[{"text":"The Sun is the star located at the centre of the Solar System. It is a massive sphere of hot plasma, heated to incandescence by nuclear fusion reactions in its core, radiating the energy from its surface mainly as visible light and infrared radiation, with 10% at ultraviolet energies. It is the main source of energy for life on Earth. The Sun has been an object of veneration in many cultures and a central subject of astronomical research since antiquity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun","wikidata":"Q525"},{"title":"Dress","blocks":[{"text":"A dress is a one-piece outer garment that is worn on the torso, hanging down over the legs. Dresses often consist of a bodice attached to a skirt."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Afternoon_ensemble_MET_63.212a-b_CP4.jpg/330px-Afternoon_ensemble_MET_63.212a-b_CP4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dress","wikidata":"Q200539"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Sun_dress.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Sun_dress.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Sun_dress.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Sun_dress.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Sun_dress.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Sun_dress.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sketch of a typical sundress","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASun_dress.tif"},{"srcset":